## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to architect a two region streaming pipeline with per-device anomaly scoring, real-time alerts, and durable storage. It checks stateful processing, idempotency, cross-region considerations, and testing strategy.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis regional streams for ingestion
- Lambda stateful processing with per-device rolling stats
- Anomaly detection with z-score
- SNS alerts and DynamoDB metadata for auditing
- Parquet storage in S3 with partitioning by region/date
- LocalStack testing plan and rough cost estimates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo rolling stats per device
const stats = {};
function handleEvent(evt){
  const id = evt.deviceId;
  if(!stats[id]) stats[id] = {sum:0, sumsq:0, n:0};
  const s = stats[id];
  s.n += 1;
  s.sum += evt.value;
  s.sumsq += evt.value * evt.value;
  const mean = s.sum / s.n;
  const varr = (s.sumsq - (s.sum*s.sum)/s.n) / (s.n-1 || 1);
  const std = Math.sqrt(varr);
  const z = (evt.value - mean) / (std || 1);
  if(Math.abs(z) > 3){ /* publish to SNS and log anomaly */ }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for late-arriving data or a rolling window more than 5 minutes?
- What are the trade-offs of storing per-device stats in DynamoDB vs Redis (ElastiCache) for latency and cost?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical privacy controls in streaming pipelines, enforcing field-level masking without breaking analytics.

## Key Concepts
- Field-level masking; deterministic tokens; per-stream salt
- Schema evolution with Glue Schema Registry
- PII handling in cross-region Kinesis→Lambda→S3
- Auditability via DynamoDB; LocalStack testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPiI(value, salt){
  if(!value) return value;
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const h = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  h.update(String(salt));
  h.update(value);
  return h.digest('hex').slice(0, 16);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate masking keys without downtime?
- How would you validate masking does not affect downstream aggregations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests schema-versioned validation, deduplication, and lineage in a minimal, real-world pipeline. It ensures handling of schema evolution while keeping the flow beginner-friendly.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis ingestion and Lambda processing
- Schema-versioned validation and conditional logic
- DynamoDB dedupe by composite key (deviceId+ts)
- Parquet writes to S3 partitioned by region/date/schema_version
- DLQ, CloudWatch lineage logging, backfill planning

## Code Example
```javascript
function validate(record){
  if (record.schema_version===1){
    return Boolean(record.deviceId && record.ts && record.temp);
  } else {
    return Boolean(record.deviceId && record.ts && record.temp && record.battery && record.location);
  }
}
```

